  "Question": "If \\(\\dfrac xy=\\dfrac34,\\) then the incorrect expression in the following is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{x+y}{y}=\\dfrac74\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{y}{y-x}=\\dfrac41\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{x+2y}{x}=\\dfrac{11}3\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{x}{2y}=\\dfrac38\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{x-y}{y}=\\dfrac14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(x/y=3/4\\) lets us write \\(x=3k\\) and \\(y=4k\\), where \\(k\\) is a nonzero real number. Then \\(y-x=k\\), so every denominator in the choices is nonzero.\n\nSubstituting and canceling the common factor gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x+y}{y}&=\\frac{7k}{4k}=\\frac74,\\\\\n\\frac{y}{y-x}&=\\frac{4k}{k}=4,\\\\\n\\frac{x+2y}{x}&=\\frac{11k}{3k}=\\frac{11}{3},\\\\\n\\frac{x}{2y}&=\\frac{3k}{8k}=\\frac38.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus choices A through D are correct. For E, however,\n\\[\n\\frac{x-y}{y}=\\frac{-k}{4k}=-\\frac14,\n\\]\nwhich is not \\(\\frac14\\). Therefore the incorrect expression is \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
